<title>CANADA: Newbridge takes charge, Q4 loss $0.17 shr.</title>
<headline>Newbridge takes charge, Q4 loss $0.17 shr.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr	   loss	C$0.17   profit	C$0.38</p>
<p> Net	   loss	29,696   profit	66,495</p>
<p> Revs		     441,341		  271,940</p>
<p>	   12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr	 profit	C$0,91   profit	C$1.19</p>
<p> Net	 profit     156,917   profit     202,864</p>
<p> Revs		   1,376,727		  921,244</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: Newbridge Networks Corp posted a pre-charge profit of C$0.38 in the fourth quarter ended April 30. The company decided in the quarter to switch to U.S. accounting principles (U.S. GAAP) and chose to write off C$97 million for research and development, turning its profit into a C$0.17 a share loss. In addition, according</p>
<p>to its new accounting system in the year-ago quarter, it posted earnings of C$0.38 a share.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
